 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of leaf nodes in the octree. Each leaf is visited once.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(V + F)$ where $V$ is the number of vertices and $F$ is the number of faces generated.
-*   **Performance:** Fast for sparse data due to octree pruning. Slower than flat grid methods for dense data due to recursion overhead.
-*   **Strengths:** Handles hierarchical data efficiently; supports variable resolution if octree is adaptive.
-*   **Limitations:** Produces blocky geometry; not suitable for smooth surfaces.
-*   **When to use:** When working with octree-based voxel data and blocky aesthetic is acceptable or desired.
-*   **When not to use:** When smooth surfaces are required (use Marching Cubes or Dual Contouring).
